[
    {
        "content": "<p>The following code:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Attr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Register</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">zify_simps</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>gets flagged by the whitespace linter with the message</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">extra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">space</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">This</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">part</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">code</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">zify_simps</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"bp\">'</span>\n<span class=\"n\">should</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">be</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">written</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">zify_simps</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"bp\">'</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"n\">Note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">This</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">can</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">be</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">disabled</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">style</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">whitespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which seems to be a bug in the linter? Somewhat unrelated: does the linter get deactivated in tactic files?</p>",
        "id": 590960144,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1777201555
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If I remember correctly, the linter does not exclude specifically tactic files, but</p>\n<ul>\n<li>does nothing if parsing of some modification of the command fails (which highly correlates with the command being a meta declaration)</li>\n<li>does not act on commands that contain a <code>macro_rules</code> node, which also correlates with tactic files.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 590962390,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777203475
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So, while it <em>could</em> tell you something about whitespace in tactic files, chances are that it won't.</p>",
        "id": 590962428,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777203494
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38361\">#38361</a> is the PR that is green even though given the above example, I would expect the linter to fire</p>",
        "id": 590962738,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1777203669
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>not too important though - I care slightly more about the linter misbehaving in the example</p>",
        "id": 590962808,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1777203760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Regarding the bug: I prefer to think of the linter as \"exposing pretty-printing\" bugs.  In this case, I view the linter complaining about something that should be changed about how <code>zify_simp</code> displays spaces.</p>",
        "id": 590971428,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777211760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/JovanGerb/lean4/blob/d695014cde255d059c4169cfd277e4a766713cd4/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Simp/RegisterCommand.lean#L27-L28\">https://github.com/JovanGerb/lean4/blob/d695014cde255d059c4169cfd277e4a766713cd4/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Simp/RegisterCommand.lean#L27-L28</a></p>\n<p>This line of code is at fault, giving the wrong spacing around the arrows.</p>",
